From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, ntdll, start: an elevated program gets its arguments as the caller wrote them

ShellExecuteEx "runas" on Windows hands lpParameters to the elevated program
verbatim. Here the SgElevate relay passed the command to sg-elevate as
separate arguments (CommandLineToArgvW's), and the Wine loader in the elevated
process wrote the command line again from them, which moves quotes: advpack's
LaunchINFSectionEx "C:\P F\x.inf",DefaultUninstall arrived as
"C:\P F\x.inf,DefaultUninstall" (Notepad2's uninstaller then left everything in
place), an MSI's PROP="a b" as "PROP=a b", blanks between arguments collapsed.

shell32: when writing the arguments again (ntdll's rules) would not give back
the caller's text, SgElevate passes it as one argument after the program,
"/sg-raw-args:TEXT" (NSIS's /UAC: still left out). Plain arguments and quoted
paths, which the loader writes back the same, go as before, so the consent
prompt shows them as before.
ntdll: build_initial_params takes "/sg-raw-args:TEXT" as the only argument after
the program as TEXT for the command line's arguments, unchanged.
start.exe: the same in /exec mode, where the loader starts a program it cannot
load itself (a .cmd) through start.exe.
The program, who is asked, the prompt and its answer are unchanged.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -2098,6 +2098,10 @@
  *
  * Build process parameters from scratch, for processes without a parent.
  */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_RAW_ARGS
+static const WCHAR sg_raw_argsW[] = {'/','s','g','-','r','a','w','-','a','r','g','s',':',0};
+#endif
+
 static RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *build_initial_params( void **module )
 {
     static const WCHAR valueW[] = {'1',0};
@@ -2154,6 +2158,33 @@
 
     main_wargv = build_wargv( get_dos_path( image ));
     cmdline = build_command_line( main_wargv );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_RAW_ARGS
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 8400): "/sg-raw-args:TEXT" as the only argument after the
+     * program is TEXT as the command line's arguments, unchanged. The elevation relay (shell32's
+     * SgElevate) passes a program's arguments so when writing them again here from separate
+     * arguments would move the caller's quotes, as Windows hands lpParameters over verbatim. */
+    if (main_wargv[0] && main_wargv[1] && !main_wargv[2] &&
+        !wcsncmp( main_wargv[1], sg_raw_argsW, ARRAY_SIZE(sg_raw_argsW) - 1 ))
+    {
+        WCHAR *prog = build_command_line( (WCHAR *[]){ main_wargv[0], NULL } );
+        const WCHAR *raw = main_wargv[1] + ARRAY_SIZE(sg_raw_argsW) - 1;
+        WCHAR *full = prog ? malloc( (wcslen( prog ) + wcslen( raw ) + 2) * sizeof(WCHAR) ) : NULL;
+
+        if (full)
+        {
+            wcscpy( full, prog );
+            if (*raw)
+            {
+                WCHAR *end = full + wcslen( full );
+                *end++ = ' ';
+                wcscpy( end, raw );
+            }
+            free( cmdline );
+            cmdline = full;
+        }
+        free( prog );
+    }
+#endif
 
     TRACE( "image %s cmdline %s dir %s\n",
            debugstr_w(main_wargv[0]), debugstr_w(cmdline), debugstr_w(curdir) );
--- a/dlls/shell32/shlexec.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shlexec.c
